-- title:
--   Gauss measure is concentrated on the open unit interval
-- statement:
--   Let $\lambda$ be Lebesgue measure on $\mathbb R$, and let
--   $\lambda_0$ be its restriction to $(0,1)$. The Gauss measure is
--   $$d\mu_G(x)=\frac{1}{\log2\,(1+x)}\,d\lambda_0(x).$$
--   Write $w(x)=1/(\log2\,(1+x))$ and $P(x)=\log(1+x)/\log2$ for $x\geq0$.
--   For $\mu_G$-almost every $x$, one has $0<x<1$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/l46430640-del/ERA-STATISTICS-FORMAL/blob/d74c241819f896ab8d050b21ace80c8e90eabd9e/BianchiIX/Statistics/GaussMeasure.lean#L97-L98

